      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "to clarify and reiterate OP's request (instead of making a new request thread):\n\nrequesting a physbone option within the SDK, that allows the bone segment that was grabbed to follow the rotation of the hand that grabbed it (up to the physbones defined angle limit). current user solution is a fairly complicated prefab, with odd and unwieldy behavior, and limited functionality. developer solution may be as simple as a well-configured constraint.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-04-29T20:51:57.940Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Unless I'm mistaken, there's currently no way to rotate a grabbed Phys Bone with your hand, i.e. handing someone a face-down card on a bone and allowing them to grab it and flip it over face-up. Can there be an option to allow rotations like this?",
